title: Microsoft Azure: Usage Details (costs) (deprecated)
agents: azure
catalog: cloud/azure
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check and the associated special agent (agent_azure) are deprecated
 and will be removed in a future version.

 Please configure the new special agent using the "Microsoft Azure" ruleset.

 This check reports the daily costs of the Azure subscription, in total
 and per Azure service type. On the host of a monitored resource group,
 it reports only the costs of that resource group.

 Cost information has a granularity of one day. The value shows
 the costs of the previous day (00:00 - 23:59 UTC).

 Azure needs up to 72 hours to collect all usage for a day. Until then,
 the reported value is an estimate: it can rise from one check cycle to the
 next, and some Azure service types may still have no costs, so their
 services show no data. Azure does not report when a value is final.

 Checkmk stores the value it gets at each check and does not update it
 later. Since the previous day is always less than 72 hours old, the
 stored values are estimates and can be lower than the final costs.
 Keep this in mind when you read the cost graphs or set levels.

 You can set levels on this value with the rule
 "Azure usage details (costs)".

item:
 The name of the Azure service type, or 'Summary' for the total costs.

discovery:
 One service is created for each Azure service type, plus one summary
 service. These services are created on the host that runs the special
 agent and on every host that corresponds to a monitored resource group.
